Why this license and not an open-source one

The AirPlay 2 protocol logic in this repository -- HomeKit pairing, the RTSP
control plane, the audio pipeline and the playout timing engine -- is a port of
rbouteiller/airplay-esp32 (https://github.com/rbouteiller/airplay-esp32), which
is published under the Non-Commercial License reproduced above. A derivative
work cannot grant rights its source did not grant, so this repository carries
the same terms. It is not OSI-approved open source, and it cannot be
relicensed under MIT or Apache-2.0 without the upstream author's permission.

Practical consequences:

  * Personal and hobby use, modification and redistribution are permitted.
  * Commercial use -- selling devices with this firmware, or shipping it in a
    product -- requires written permission from Remi Bouteiller.
  * This component cannot be merged into the ESPHome monorepo, which is
    permissively licensed. See components/airplay_receiver/UPSTREAMING.md.

Third-party components carry their own licenses; see THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md.
